A COMPLETE RUN CONTAINING ONE INCOMPLETE REPORT.  Expected verdict: 1.

Read this one against no-suite-summary.log; they are the two halves of the same
question and they must not be confused.

  * HERE, the run finished -- the suite's summary line is present -- but one
    report inside it lost its stacks.  With continue_on_error=1 the reports are
    written from a signal-ish context while the suite keeps printing to the same
    handle, so an interleaved write can land in the middle of a stack dump and
    the frames simply are not there.  There is a report and nothing to
    attribute it to, so it is OURS: exit 1, gate red.

  * IN no-suite-summary.log, the run itself died.  There is no summary line, so
    there is nothing to attribute anything to -- not this report, not the
    reports that would have come later, not the tests that never ran.  That is
    exit 3, and it is a different failure with a different fix.

Do not "simplify" these two into one case.  The distinction is exactly the one
the integrity sentinel adds, and a fixture set that cannot tell a damaged
report from a dead run cannot tell whether the sentinel still works.

